    "thesis": {
      "date": "2015-12-31",
      "title": "Multiple Impedance Control of Hybrid Parallel-Serial Manipulator for Object Manipulation",
      "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/379480054_Multiple_Impedance_Control_of_Hybrid_Parallel-Serial_Manipulator_for_Object_Manipulation",
      "abstract": "One of the widely used of industrial robots is object manipulation (OM). Cable driven parallel robot (CDPR) has a very large workspace suitable for this application. However, there are possible cable collisions with the environment. Therefore, use of a Serial Manipulator (SM) is recommended penetrating the blind spots. Thus, the combination of CDPR-SM is recommended for OM. The tasks of OM, welding, surface finishing, cleaning, etc. need algorithms capable of determining the interaction force and position. In addition, constrained and suspended structure of CDPR is evaluated and the best structure for the control and construction is selected. Kinematics modeling of robots include CDPR and SM are provided. Topics such as inverse kinematics, Jacobian, velocity, acceleration analysis, singularity and sensitivity of CDPR are investigated. Also forward, inverse kinematics, velocity, acceleration, Jacobian, singularities and workspace analysis of SM are checked. Dynamics model for using in control subjects; simulation and system analysis take place. The SM dynamics is obtained by iterative Newton-Euler and CDPR dynamics is modeled by Newton-Euler method. An algorithm to optimize traction cable is also provided. In addition, a redundancy resolution algorithm is provided. However, a new method is proposed to reduce the redundancy of actuators. A virtual model verifies the equation. Structure of CDPR equipped with SM is optimized by criteria such as controllable, free singularity workspace, sensitivity and stiffness. Multiple impedance control (MIC) is used to OM in the presence of external disturbances. Also parallel and serial MIC with different coefficient is implemented. However, work and joint space unit impedance is also checked. Coefficients are optimised by error and wrench criteria. The CDPR, which discussed in this thesis for implementing control algorithms and studying performance is manufactured. According to the analysis, mechanical components of the robot are designed. In addition, electronic platform is prepared to send control commands. The pose of platform is obtained by a new method that combines machine vision and winch angles. The artificial neural network is trained for forward kinematics."
    },
